  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'd like to recommend an upgrade to how fallback avatars are selected. I'd like to recommend the option to select a general fallback which will by default be used for all of your avatars. But with the ability to override this on an individual avatar so that you can choose a specific fallback avatar for that avatar.\nSay for example you've made multiple fallback avatars that match your full scale avatars you'd only be able to select a singular one. With the upgrade you'd be able to match fallbacks to avatars.\nMy personal use case for this system is that I've made a fallback with a generic \"please show my avatar\" message on it. However in cases where I'm using a PC only avatar if a quest user attempts to show it they'll see no change. So I'd like to be able to define a different fallback tied to those pc only avatars that mention that there is no quest version available or at the least a fallback that matches thematically.",
